# Included articles

## Summary

The articles filed under a subcategory that has no subcategories of its own, listed page by page. The articles belong to the project's articles module; this tab only lists them, and opens one where the project has that module.

## Requirements

- **ARTLIST** — The tab lists the articles filed under the category that are not archived, 10 to a page (10, 20, 30 or 50 can be chosen), newest first until a column is sorted. Sorting and paging happen on the backend.
- **ARTCOLUMNS** — Each article shows its name in the admin's language, its SAP-ID where the articles have one, whether it is active, and its type. Where the articles configuration (`juicecommerce:articles`) sets `showPublicStatus`, it also shows whether the article is public, and a private article with a privacy reason is marked "Missing name translation".
- **ARTFILTER** — The name and the SAP-ID can be filtered by typing; the list follows once typing pauses, from its first page. The name is searched in the language of the articles shown.
- **ARTOPEN** — Where the project has an articles module, an article's name opens its details.

## Tests

- A category with 25 articles shows 10 on the first page and 3 pages in all.
- Typing part of an article's name leaves only matching articles, starting again from page 1.
- Without an articles module in the project, the names are plain text.

## Record: Article

### Summary

An article of the project's shop, as far as this tab shows it. It is kept by the articles module, outside this model.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required unique
name: map(string) required
active: boolean
public: boolean
type: string
sapId: string
privacyReason: list(string)
categories: list(juicebar.categories#Category)
archived: boolean
```

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/categories/categories.types.ts#CategoryArticle` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## View: IncludedArticles

### Summary

The Included articles tab of an opened subcategory.

### Display

- The category's articles, page by page, with name, SAP-ID, status, public and type — [reads](aim:juicebar.categories.articles#Record:Article), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.articles#Requirements[ARTLIST]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.articles#Requirements[ARTCOLUMNS])
- Filters on name and SAP-ID — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.articles#Requirements[ARTFILTER])
- Each name links to the article's page in the articles module, where the project has one — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.articles#Requirements[ARTOPEN])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/categories/details/included-articles/included-articles.component.ts#IncludedArticlesComponent` — as: component
- binds: `service:juicecommerce:articles#fetch` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
